  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14190079/assets/f822ed2c39270fde5dfea6fa50c6985a837b45160c6f5366636d04c5908c5790.png)\n\nWhat are the roots of the function $f(x)$ defined by the mapping diagram shown above?\n\nIn **ascending order**, the roots are $x=$\n{{field-1}}\nand $x=$\n{{field-2}}.",
  "worked_solution": "The roots of the function are the values of $x$ such that $f(x)=0.$ In the given mapping diagram, we see that $f(-2)=0$ and $f(-1)=0.$\n\nTherefore, the roots of the function are $x=-2$ and $x=-1.$",
